    "story": [
      "the four frames are swimlanes, one per owner: Support, Billing service, Payments (Stripe), Ledger; the lane a step sits in is who does it, even if the step was drawn into the lane rather than attached to it",
      "Support owns 'refund request ticket' and 'agent approves'; Billing service owns 'check 30-day window', 'create refund' and 'mark order refunded'; Stripe owns 'POST /v1/refunds' and 'charge.refunded webhook'; Ledger owns 'credit note'",
      "they first put 'check 30-day window' in the Support lane, then moved it down to Billing service: billing rejects old refunds, support does not check",
      "arrows that cross a lane are handoffs between teams: Support to Billing, Billing to Stripe, Stripe back to Billing (the webhook), Billing to Ledger",
      "they believe the webhook, not the API response, marks the order refunded, but are only about 70% sure",
      "orange means external (Stripe's side), said aloud; there is no drawn legend",
      "'email customer' is dashed, sits across the gap between the Billing service and Payments lanes, in neither, with a '?' beside it and circled: they do not know who sends the refund email",
      "the pen underline is under 'check 30-day window' (said aloud: unsure it is 30 days for annual plans)"
    ],
    "partner_should_ask_about": [
      "who sends the refund email: a support macro, billing on the webhook, or Stripe's receipt",
      "does the webhook or the API response mark the order refunded",
      "is the window 30 days for every plan (annual plans)",
      "what happens when the 30-day check fails (no arrow for rejection)"
    ]
  }
